# Skywalker X8 flying wing (sim/models/skywalker_x8).
#
# The gazebo-zephyr frame is used because it is the only ArduPlane frame marked
# `external`, i.e. the only one that hands flight dynamics to Gazebo. Its
# defaults are for the Zephyr though, and they reverse both elevons — the X8
# model's ArduPilotPlugin expects them un-reversed, so left/right roll and pitch
# would come out backwards without these.
SERVO1_FUNCTION 77
SERVO2_FUNCTION 78
SERVO1_REVERSED 0
SERVO2_REVERSED 0

# Travel limits matching the <control> blocks in the model.
SERVO1_MIN 1100
SERVO1_MAX 1900
SERVO1_TRIM 1500
SERVO2_MIN 1100
SERVO2_MAX 1900
SERVO2_TRIM 1500

# Pusher motor.
SERVO3_FUNCTION 70
SERVO3_MIN 1000
SERVO3_MAX 2000
SERVO3_TRIM 1000

# No airspeed sensor on the model. Keep it that way.
#
# ARSPD_TYPE 100 (the SITL backend) was tried and is WRONG here: it derives
# airspeed from SITL's own aircraft model, which does not run when Gazebo owns
# the physics. Measured with it enabled: reported airspeed 1.0 m/s while the
# aircraft was rolling at 18.4 m/s groundspeed. TECS concluded it was stationary
# and never rotated -- full throttle down the strip, no takeoff at all. Strictly
# worse than no sensor.
#
# So TECS runs on synthetic airspeed from GPS + attitude, and the AIRSPEED_*
# values below are targets for that estimate rather than a measured feedback
# loop. That is a real limitation, not a tuning choice: it is why throttle
# control on the climb-out is loose.
ARSPD_TYPE 0

# Ground takeoff on a belly-lander. Do not wait for a hand-launch acceleration
# spike, and hold the nose down until there is enough speed to rotate — without
# this the wing tries to lift before it is flying and drops a tip.
TKOFF_THR_MINACC 0
TKOFF_THR_DELAY 0
TKOFF_ROTATE_SPD 12

# --- Cruise speed -----------------------------------------------------------
# There is no airspeed sensor on the model (ARSPD_TYPE 0), so ArduPlane flies
# on synthetic airspeed from GPS + attitude. These bound it low: the X8 will
# cruise around 14 m/s rather than the ~20+ the defaults aim for.
# Slow, but not underpowered: capping THR_MAX at 75 and trimming to 35 left it
# unable to sustain the climb — it reached 45 m, ran out of energy and sank
# back onto the strip. Full throttle stays available for climbing; the cruise
# speed is set by the airspeed targets, not by starving the motor.
#
# NAMES MATTER HERE. These were TRIM_ARSPD_CM / ARSPD_FBW_MIN / ARSPD_FBW_MAX
# until ArduPlane 4.5 renamed them. ArduPilot ignores a parameter it does not
# recognise WITHOUT ERROR, so the old names loaded cleanly, printed nothing,
# and left the firmware on its defaults: cruise 12 m/s and min 9 m/s instead of
# the 15 and 13 tuned here.
#
# That is what made TAKEOFF fail. TECS dutifully held the 12 m/s it had been
# left with, which this wing cannot sustain in a climb; it topped out at 56 m,
# decayed to 11.8 m/s and sank back onto the strip with the throttle being
# pulled back the whole way. It reads exactly like an underpowered airframe or
# a stall, which is why it is worth stating plainly: nothing was wrong with the
# aircraft, three parameters were simply not being applied.
#
# Check with `param show AIRSPEED_*` after a firmware bump rather than trusting
# the file — a rename is silent, and the symptom appears in flight, not at boot.
#
# Note the unit change: TRIM_ARSPD_CM was cm/s (1500), AIRSPEED_CRUISE is m/s.
AIRSPEED_CRUISE 15
AIRSPEED_MIN 13
AIRSPEED_MAX 22
# Raised from 45. With no airspeed sensor TECS has no speed loop: throttle is
# height demand plus this as feedforward. At 45 the wing could not hold level
# flight at cruise, so it climbed to ~55 m, ran the throttle down to 23 and
# sank. This is the cruise-power assumption, not a limit -- THR_MAX stays 100.
TRIM_THROTTLE 65
THR_MAX 100

# Demanding 5 m/s from a wing that only achieves ~2.9 m/s made TECS trade speed
# it did not have for climb it could not deliver.
TECS_CLMB_MAX 3

# --- Holding pattern --------------------------------------------------------
# TAKEOFF climbs to TKOFF_ALT and then holds; LOITER circles wherever it is.
# A 120 m radius at ~14 m/s is a comfortable ~55 s orbit for this wing.
TKOFF_ALT 60
WP_LOITER_RAD 120
# LOITER_RAD does not exist on ArduPlane -- WP_LOITER_RAD above is the one
# that applies. Left here as a note so it is not re-added.

# --- Wings level off the strip ----------------------------------------------
# It was dropping the left wing on the climb-out. Hold wings level until well
# clear of the ground, and bias roll slightly right to cancel the residual.
TKOFF_LVL_ALT 25
RLL2SRV_RMAX 45

# No terrain database. SITL has no terrain tiles to consult, and the altitude
# reaching ArduPilot is inflated by the world's ground height (SIM_Gazebo adds
# home_alt to a Gazebo z that already measures from sea level). The terrain
# subsystem then logs "Terrain: clamping offset 152 to 30" and GUIDED takeoff
# is refused. Nothing here needs terrain following.
TERRAIN_ENABLE 0
TERRAIN_FOLLOW 0
